<title>USA: FERC sees no major market issue in IES deal.</title>
<headline>FERC sees no major market issue in IES deal.</headline>
<dateline>CEDAR RAPIDS, Iowa 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) has found no substantive market power concerns in a proposed merger between IES Industries Inc, Interstate Power Co and WPL Holdings Inc, according to a statement from IES.</p>
<p>IES said the commmission expects to rule on the merger application in the third quarter of this year.</p>
<p>FERC also called a hearing to address remaining technical issues in the merger, IES said.</p>
<p>The three companies announced plans to merge in November and form a new company called Interstate Energy Corp.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk, 212/859-1700))</p>
</text>
